#: _CompositeMeasureScoring
msgid "CompositeMeasureScoring"
msgstr ""

# null
#: _CompositeMeasureScoring@definition
msgid "Observation values that communicate the method used in a quality measure to combine the component measure results included in an composite measure."
msgstr ""

# null
#: ALLORNONESCR
msgid "All-or-nothing Scoring"
msgstr ""

# null
#: ALLORNONESCR@definition
msgid "Code specifying that the measure uses all-or-nothing scoring. All-or-nothing scoring places an individual in the numerator of the composite measure if and only if they are in the numerator of all component measures in which they are in the denominator."
msgstr ""

# null
#: LINEARSCR
msgid "Linear Scoring"
msgstr ""

# null
#: LINEARSCR@definition
msgid "Code specifying that the measure uses linear scoring. Linear scoring computes the fraction of component measures in which the individual appears in the numerator, giving equal weight to each component measure."
msgstr ""

# null
#: OPPORSCR
msgid "Opportunity Scoring"
msgstr ""

# null
#: OPPORSCR@definition
msgid "Code specifying that the measure uses opportunity-based scoring. In opportunity-based scoring the measure score is determined by combining the denominator and numerator of each component measure to determine an overall composite score."
msgstr ""

# null
#: WEIGHTSCR
msgid "Weighted Scoring"
msgstr ""

# null
#: WEIGHTSCR@definition
msgid "Code specifying that the measure uses weighted scoring. Weighted scoring assigns a factor to each component measure to weight that measure's contribution to the overall score."
msgstr ""

