#: _CommonClinicalObservationResultValue@definition
msgid "**Definition:** The non-laboratory, non-diagnostic imaging coded result of the coded observable or \"question\" represented by the paired concept from the the NonLabDICodedObservationType domain.

\]

**Examples:**An APGAR result, a functional assessment, etc. The value must not require a specific unit of measure."
msgstr "!!"

# null
#: _CoverageChemicalDependencyValue
msgid "CoverageChemicalDependencyValue"
msgstr ""

# null
#: _CoverageChemicalDependencyValue@definition
msgid "**Definition:** The category of addiction used for coverage purposes that may refer to a substance, the consumption of which may result in physical or emotional harm."
msgstr ""

# null
#: _IndividualCaseSafetyReportValueDomains
msgid "Individual Case Safety Report Value Domains"
msgstr ""

# null
#: _IndividualCaseSafetyReportValueDomains@definition
msgid "This domain is established as a parent to a variety of value domains being defined to support the communication of Individual Case Safety Reports to regulatory bodies. Arguably, this aggregation is not taxonomically pure, but the grouping will facilitate the management of these domains."
msgstr ""

# null
#: _CaseSeriousnessCriteria
msgid "CaseSeriousnessCriteria"
msgstr ""

# null (!!when last translated was: A code that provides information on the overall effect or outcome of the adverse reaction/adverse event reported in the ICSR. Note the criterion applies to the case as a whole and not to an individual reaction.)
#: _CaseSeriousnessCriteria@definition
msgid "A code that provides information on the overall effect or outcome of the adverse reaction/adverse event reported in the ICSR. Note the criterion applies to the case as a whole and not to an individual reaction.

Example concepts are: death, disability, hospitalization, congenital anomaly/ birth defect, and other medically important condition."
msgstr "!!"

# null
#: _DeviceManufacturerEvaluationInterpretation
msgid "DeviceManufacturerEvaluationInterpretation"
msgstr ""

# null (!!when last translated was: A code set that includes codes that are used to characterize the outcome of the device evaluation process. The code defines the manufacturer's conclusions following the evaluation.)
#: _DeviceManufacturerEvaluationInterpretation@definition
msgid "A code set that includes codes that are used to characterize the outcome of the device evaluation process. The code defines the manufacturer's conclusions following the evaluation.

Examples include: inadequate alarms, device maintenance contributed to event, device failed just prior to use, user error caused event"
msgstr "!!"

# null
#: _DeviceManufacturerEvaluationMethod
msgid "DeviceManufacturerEvaluationMethod"
msgstr ""

# null (!!when last translated was: Code assigned to indicate a relevant fact within the context of the evaluation of a reported product. There are a number of concept types including the status of the evaluation, the type of evaluation findings, and the type of activity carried out as part of the evaluation process.)
#: _DeviceManufacturerEvaluationMethod@definition
msgid "Code assigned to indicate a relevant fact within the context of the evaluation of a reported product. There are a number of concept types including the status of the evaluation, the type of evaluation findings, and the type of activity carried out as part of the evaluation process.

Examples include: Actual device involved in incident was evaluated, electrical tests performed, visual examination."
msgstr "!!"

# null
#: _DeviceManufacturerEvaluationResult
msgid "DeviceManufacturerEvaluationResult"
msgstr ""

# null (!!when last translated was: Code assigned to indicate an outcome of the manufacturer's investigation of a product for which a defect has been reported.)
#: _DeviceManufacturerEvaluationResult@definition
msgid "Code assigned to indicate an outcome of the manufacturer's investigation of a product for which a defect has been reported.

Examples include:.component/subassembly failure: air cleaner, computer-, imaging system-, microprocessor-controlled device problem: cache memory, design -- not fail safe."
msgstr "!!"

# null
#: _PertinentReactionRelatedness
msgid "Pertinent Reaction Relatedness"
msgstr ""

# null (!!when last translated was: A code to capture the reporter's assessment of the extent to which the reaction is related to the suspect product reported in the ICSR.)
#: _PertinentReactionRelatedness@definition
msgid "A code to capture the reporter's assessment of the extent to which the reaction is related to the suspect product reported in the ICSR.

Example concepts include: related, not related, possibly related and unlikely related."
msgstr "!!"

# null
#: _ProductCharacterization
msgid "Product Characterization"
msgstr ""

# null (!!when last translated was: A code that characterizes the role that the primary reporter felt that the suspect intervention -- either a substance administration or a device related procedure - played in the incident being reported. This code will capture the primary reporter's assessment of the role that the suspect product played in the incident reported in the ICSR.)
#: _ProductCharacterization@definition
msgid "A code that characterizes the role that the primary reporter felt that the suspect intervention -- either a substance administration or a device related procedure - played in the incident being reported. This code will capture the primary reporter's assessment of the role that the suspect product played in the incident reported in the ICSR.

Examples include: Suspect, Concomitant, Interacting, Re-challenge."
msgstr "!!"

# null
#: _ReactionActionTaken
msgid "ReactionActionTaken"
msgstr ""

# null (!!when last translated was: Code used to indicate the action taken by practitioner in response to the problem (whether drug or device related) that is reported in the ICSR.)
#: _ReactionActionTaken@definition
msgid "Code used to indicate the action taken by practitioner in response to the problem (whether drug or device related) that is reported in the ICSR.

Examples include: failing device replaced, medication stopped, medication dose adjusted."
msgstr "!!"

# null
#: _SubjectReaction
msgid "Subject Reaction"
msgstr ""

# null (!!when last translated was: A code to capture the kind of reaction that was suffered by the investigated subject, and that is being reported in the ICSR. At this point, SNOMED or MedDRA have been suggested as code systems to be used for providing this information.)
#: _SubjectReaction@definition
msgid "A code to capture the kind of reaction that was suffered by the investigated subject, and that is being reported in the ICSR. At this point, SNOMED or MedDRA have been suggested as code systems to be used for providing this information.

Example concepts include hives, swelling, rash, anaphylactic shock."
msgstr "!!"

# null
#: _SubjectReactionEmphasis
msgid "SubjectReactionEmphasis"
msgstr ""

# null (!!when last translated was: Code that captures the emphasis that the reporter placed on this reaction.)
#: _SubjectReactionEmphasis@definition
msgid "Code that captures the emphasis that the reporter placed on this reaction.

Examples include: highlighted by the reporter, NOT serious, Not highlighted by the reporter, NOT serious, Highlighted by the reporter, SERIOUS, Not highlighted by the reporter, SERIOUS."
msgstr "!!"

# null
#: _SubjectReactionOutcome
msgid "SubjectReactionOutcome"
msgstr ""

# null (!!when last translated was: Code that captures the type of outcome from an individual outcome of a reaction to the suspect product reported in the ICSR.)
#: _SubjectReactionOutcome@definition
msgid "Code that captures the type of outcome from an individual outcome of a reaction to the suspect product reported in the ICSR.

Examples include: Recovered/resolved. Recovering/resolving, Not recovered/not resolved, Recovered/resolved with sequelae, Fatal."
msgstr "!!"

